     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi All,<div> I have been developing a stock assessment package using TMB and fit the models using Jim Thorson&#39;s &quot;fit_tmb&quot; code (<a href=\"https://github.com/kaskr/TMB_contrib_R/tree/master/TMBhelper/R\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/kaskr/TMB_contrib_R/tree/master/TMBhelper/R&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792462275638000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2_cC_d-mkklYpSLyzBOClh\">https://github.com/kaskr/TMB_contrib_R/tree/master/TMBhelper/R</a>) and have found that when I fit a specific model using my Mac, I can get the standard errors of the derived quantities successfully from the sdrep function. However, when I fit the exact same model/code on my PC, the sdrep function returns <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(36,41,46);font-family:SFMono-Regular,Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,Menlo,monospace;font-size:12px;white-space:pre\">pdHess</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(215,58,73);font-family:SFMono-Regular,Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,Menlo,monospace;font-size:12px;white-space:pre\">==</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,92,197);font-family:SFMono-Regular,Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,Menlo,monospace;font-size:12px;white-space:pre\">TRUE</span>, but all the standard errors of the derived quantities are NaN. Has anyone else found differences in model outputs between PC/MAC?</div><div>Thanks,</div><div>Grant</div><div><div><br></div>-- <br><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_signature\" data-smartmail=\"gmail_signature\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div style=\"color:rgb(136,136,136);font-size:12.8px\"><span style=\"font-size:small\"><u><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">Grant Adams</font></u></span></div><div><font size=\"2\" color=\"#000000\" face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">School of Aquatic Fishery Sciences<br></font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-